# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values.
# In production (Vercel), set these in Project Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# NOTE: every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is inlined at BUILD time. Changing one in Vercel
# has no effect until you redeploy.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION — without this, every lead is silently lost.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Sheets storage: the Apps Script web app URL (see SETUP.md, step 1).
# Vercel's filesystem is ephemeral, so the Sheet is the ONLY durable place a lead
# is written in production. If this is unset or wrong, /api/lead logs
# "LEAD ... WAS NOT STORED ANYWHERE" and the visitor is told their details didn't
# save and asked to book a time instead.
SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL=

# REQUIRED whenever SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL is set. Must match the SECRET constant in
# the Apps Script. Without it, anyone who discovers the /exec URL can write rows
# into your leads Sheet and trigger notification emails from your account.
SHEETS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Booking
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public scheduler link shown after a successful intake submission.
# MUST be the same Google Calendar booking page as the operating system's
# canonical link in 00_CONTROL_CENTER/sender_identity.yaml — there is only ever
# one live link. The appointment-schedule slot length must be 15 minutes, which is
# what the site copy tells visitors.
# (Also works with Calendly or Cal.com, which the booking step embeds inline.)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_URL — REMOVED. The booking link is now hardcoded in lib/site.ts
# so the site and the outbound email signature can never point at different calendars.
# If this variable is still set in Vercel, DELETE it; it is ignored either way.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Legal identity — set these as soon as the business details exist
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A privacy policy has to name who is responsible for the data and give a contact
# route that isn't the sales form. Both are left blank rather than invented; the
# privacy page degrades to "available on request" until they are filled in.
# Public inbox for privacy/legal requests, e.g. hello@yourdomain.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=
# Registered entity and jurisdiction, e.g. "Example Lead Growth LLC, New Jersey, USA"
NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_ENTITY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SEO
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical site URL (used for SEO / social card links). Use the STABLE Vercel
# production URL (no custom domain). This is also the built-in default in lib/site.ts;
# only override it here / in Vercel if you later add a real custom domain.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL — REMOVED. The canonical origin is hardcoded in lib/site.ts
# (https://www.b2bleadgrowth.com). If this is still set in Vercel, DELETE it.
